# HOST-level cron jobs for linux-claw.
# Install with: crontab deploy/crontab   (run as the `claw` user, from ~/career-ops)
# View installed jobs with: crontab -l
# Remove with: crontab -r
#
# The discovery/scanning itself now runs on ITS OWN schedule INSIDE the
# career-ops container (deploy/container-crontab, loaded automatically by
# container-start.sh -- part of the Docker config, no separate install step
# needed for that half). This host crontab now only carries the git
# commit+push step (deploy/git-sync-portals.sh), which needs the host's SSH
# deploy key and so can't run inside the container. Daily, not weekly: it's
# fast (no scanning), and picks up whatever the container's weekly run
# produced without a week-long wait to push it.
#
# deploy/discover-companies.sh (the older host-triggered, docker-compose-exec
# version) still exists for manually triggering a full run from the host in
# one shot -- just isn't on this schedule anymore, to avoid running the
# discovery twice (once in-container, once via this host script).

0 8 * * * cd /home/claw/career-ops && ./deploy/git-sync-portals.sh >> /home/claw/career-ops/deploy/discover.log 2>&1
